<%#
  What one cell of this matrix stands for, and what "no change" means (WP5).

  Rendered above the matrix on the administration screens, where a selection
  covers several trackers, roles and projects at once and a single click can
  therefore write a great many rules. A project's own matrix is one tracker,
  one role and one project by construction, so there is nothing to say and
  nothing is shown.

  The sentence about row and column actions is only for the matrix that has
  them: the field-permissions matrix renders core's own "no change" cells but no
  row or column actions, so there it would explain a control that is not on the
  page. Locals: rule_type.

  Rendered from the scope panel rather than from an anchor of its own: the panel
  is already inserted directly above the matrix on both administration screens,
  and this belongs in the same place. Unlike the panel it does not depend on a
  project being selected -- core's own "no change" cells appear for a selection
  of several trackers or roles alone.
%>
<% selection_size = project_workflow_selection_size %>
<% if selection_size > 1 %>
  <p class="project-workflow-bulk-note">
    <%= l(:text_project_workflow_bulk_selection,
          count: selection_size,
          trackers: Array(@trackers).size,
          roles: Array(@roles).size,
          scopes: project_workflow_selection_scopes) %>
    <em>
      <%= l(:text_project_workflow_bulk_legend, no_change: l(:label_no_change_option)) %>
      <% if rule_type == ProjectWorkflowScope::TRANSITIONS %>
        <%= l(:text_project_workflow_bulk_legend_actions, no_change: l(:label_no_change_option)) %>
      <% end %>
    </em>
  </p>
<% end %>
